msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:21
msgid "What is included in Nix's Docker image?"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:23
msgid ""
"The official Docker image is created using `pkgs.dockerTools."
"buildLayeredImage` (and not with `Dockerfile` as it is usual with Docker "
"images). You can still base your custom Docker image on it as you would do "
"with any other Docker image."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:28
msgid ""
"The Docker image is not based on any other image and includes a minimal set "
"of runtime dependencies that are required to use Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:32
msgid "Docker image with the latest development version of Nix"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:34
msgid ""
"To get the latest image that was built by [Hydra](https://hydra.nixos.org) "
"run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-docker.md:37
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ curl -L https://hydra.nixos.org/job/nix/master/dockerImage.x86_64-linux/"
"latest/download/1 | docker load\n"
"$ docker run -ti nix:2.5pre20211105\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

